# node.pin - the second implementation's interpreter, pinned by tarball digest.
#
# Why this file exists: the four outsider steps end with a pytest run in which one
# test shell-outs to `node` and skips itself when node is absent. Skipped is not
# passed. The container built for the first round of this work therefore passed
# 40 of 41 tests and said so only in a footnote - the number was reported, the
# reason was not.
#
# The fix is not "apt-get install nodejs": that would put an unpinned version,
# from an unpinned Debian snapshot, into an image whose whole claim is that the
# environment is fixed by digest. So the Node tarball itself is pinned by sha256:
#
#   https://nodejs.org/dist/v26.13.1/node-v26.13.1-linux-x64.tar.xz
#   sha256 5c063e46bab0fbc1c17cc445d7ff129cbdcd0471be6ed83b6ab864f8143bc864
#
# (v26.13.1 "Lithium" LTS, downloaded 2026-11-29; the digest was taken from
# SHASUMS256.txt published beside the file and then verified against the bytes
# actually downloaded - 34,093,052 bytes.)
#
# One reference, one place: docker/Dockerfile quotes these two lines as the ARGs
# NODE_TARBALL and NODE_SHA256, and tools/check_base_image_pin.py refuses a tree
# where the two disagree. The tarball is unpacked by docker/install-node.py with
# the standard library only, and the unpack step re-checks the digest before
# anything is extracted.

v26.13.1
https://nodejs.org/dist/v26.13.1/node-v26.13.1-linux-x64.tar.xz
sha256 5c063e46bab0fbc1c17cc445d7ff129cbdcd0471be6ed83b6ab864f8143bc864
